-- Security follow-up to #3470.
-- phaseo:allow-destructive-migration reason: the only match is the TRUNCATE privilege taken away from anon and authenticated by the REVOKE below; no table is truncated, nothing is dropped and no data is deleted.

-- gateway_requests.detail_metadata holds the web search queries, results, citations and fetched URLs of
-- each request. The API and the website hide them from members when a workspace limits stored contents to
-- owners and admins, but any member could still read the column directly through the Data API (the row
-- policy only checks membership), and through get_gateway_request_observability, which returns whole rows.
-- The apps read request logs with the service role and apply the contents setting themselves, so signed-in
-- and anonymous clients now read every column except detail_metadata, and lose the write and TRUNCATE
-- privileges they never needed (no client write policy exists; TRUNCATE ignores row policies).
-- New gateway_requests columns are not client-readable until granted here.
REVOKE ALL ON TABLE "public"."gateway_requests" FROM "anon", "authenticated";

